==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[Image:Surface anatomy of the heart.png|thumb|200px|coração]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|coraçon||heart}}, a derivative of {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|cor||heart|lang=la}} with the suffix {{term|-ção|-ação|lang=pt}}, either a {{etyl|VL.|pt}} root *''coratione'' or *''coraceone''.

Cognate with Aragonese {{term|corazón|lang=an}}, Asturian {{term|corazón|lang=ast}}, Galician {{term|corazón|lang=gl}}, Ladino {{term|korasón|lang=lad}}, Leonese {{term|corazón|lang=roa-leo}}, Mirandese {{term|coraçon|lang=mwl}}, Mozarabic {{term|corachón|lang=mxi}} and Spanish {{term|corazón|lang=es}} (Old Spanish {{term|coraçon|lang=osp}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/ko.ɾa.ˈsɐ̃w̃/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/ku.ɾɐ.ˈsɐ̃w̃/|lang=pt}}
*: {{audio|pt-pt-coração.ogg|Audio (PT)|lang=pt}}
*: {{homophones|lang=pt|curação|Curação}}
* {{hyphenation|co|ra|ção|lang=pt}}

====Noun====
{{pt-noun|m|corações}}

# {{l/en|heart}} {{gloss|organ of the body}}
